From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] seabraid: name where an expert's bytes live, and send a
 file reference (wire v9)

FileExpertSource::file_paths() is the files it reads, in the order of
file_extents(layer, expert, out[3], n): one extent for experts.bin, three
(gate, up, down) for the GGUF in place, each {file index, length, offset}.
The extents come from spans(), the function copy_from_files and the page-cache
probes already read, so a reader that preads them cannot disagree with the
bytes this source assembles (Span gains the file index it already knew).

RemoteExperts::seabraid_retier_file sends one kTierSwapFile: the FileRef goes
through channel blob slot 0, same fence, same residency adoption and same
fail-closed rules as seabraid_retier_blob. Main validates the ref with the wire's
one file_ref_valid before it submits, and refuses a helper that announced
file_io 0. Results: kTierApplied; kTierRejected (use bytes); kTierBadSum (the
helper read other bytes than the manifest); kTierFailed (closes the card).

file_expert_source_test proves, for every cell of a synthetic canonical pack,
that the bytes at file_extents are the bytes copy_blob assembles, and that a
cell outside the model or a closed source names nothing.
